                    },
                    "message": "Any more pointers for this kind of thing?  What is used instead?\n\nThis sounds like the \"single chassis\" option we used to have then abandoned."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "We model boards as Assemblies.. Upstream there was discussion about help in PDI to know if the board should be modeled as an assembly or a chassis.. But I think the first step would be getting Assemblies in\n\nThis is also slightly different than the \"single chassis\" because we have multiple chassis, just not boards as chassis.\n\nAlthough I could be moved by an argument of \"this helps downstream forks carry patches\", I am more moved by the fact this information is repeated 10+ times. This is a best practices commit IMO."
                },
                {
